  "limitations": [
    "The shared epoch itself was not recorded. The epoch estimate is an inferred upper bound from first observed service arrivals; lane.start denotes pre-barrier entry. Relative drift can be negative against this proxy.",
    "Actual export/governance median separation is approximately500ms and AI/governance approximately250ms in both runs; service overlap is correlation, not proof of a particular blocking task.",
    "Service CPU covers each entire observed operation. Outer-minus-original figures subtract aggregate quantiles, not paired per-operation timer overhead.",
    "Guarded callback elapsed sums exclude the nested original sampler snapshot body to avoid double counting. They include observer work and scheduling delay, and omit indirect SQL or scheduling perturbation; they are not subtractable workload CPU costs.",
    "Query age while Lock-waiting is not actual lock wait duration. A later graph and cached activity context cannot prove the exact lock holding interval or assign background task identity.",
    "Host counters cover the selected host CPU and sampled cgroup; zero steal or throttling does not establish a quiet host or exclude interference.",
    "This perturbed pair has no comparator flags. Previously failed uninstrumented comparisons remain failed; one instrumented pass does not independently establish release readiness."
